-- title:
--   Ramification datum and q-powers on principal units of R_w
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $K_w$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb{Q}_q \subseteq$ `PadicAlgCl q` (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$) that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$. Write $R_w =$ `Rw q Kw` for the valuation subring of $K_w$ obtained by pulling back, along the structure map $K_w \to$ `PadicAlgCl q`, the valuation subring attached to the canonical valuation of `PadicAlgCl q`; let $\mathfrak{m}_w =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Rw q Kw)` be its maximal ideal, and for $k \in \mathbb{N}$ let `principalUnits (Rw q Kw) k` be the subgroup of $R_w^\times$ consisting of those units $u$ with $u - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_w^{\,k}$. The assertion is the existence of natural numbers $e, f$ with $0 < e$, $0 < f$ such that: the ideal of $R_w$ generated by the image of $q$ equals $\mathfrak{m}_w^{\,e}$; the residue field `IsLocalRing.ResidueField (Rw q Kw)` has cardinality $q^f$ (as a `Nat.card`); $e f = \operatorname{finrank}_{\mathbb{Q}_q} K_w$; for every $k > e$ the image of `principalUnits (Rw q Kw) k` under the $q$-th power map on units is exactly `principalUnits (Rw q Kw) (k + e)`; and for every $k > e$, every $\zeta \in$ `principalUnits (Rw q Kw) k` with $\zeta^q = 1$ equals $1$.
--
--   This packages the ramification and inertia invariants of a finite extension $K_w/\mathbb{Q}_q$ together with the behaviour of the $q$-th power map on the filtration of principal units by one single existential, so that a consumer obtains the same exponent $e$ in all five clauses. It feeds the computation of the dimension of the invariants in [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.finrank_invariants_linHom_unitsModPow_Kw_of_basis`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.finrank_invariants_linHom_unitsModPow_Kw_of_basis), where for a tame level one reads off $q \nmid e$ from $ef = [K_w:\mathbb{Q}_q]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ExtCitation_LocalLevel_exists_ramification_principalUnits_Rw.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ExtCitation_LocalLevelResidues
import Definitions.Def_LocalRing_PrincipalUnits

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false
open ExtCitation.LocalLevel IsLocalRing

theorem ExtCitation.LocalLevel.exists_ramification_principalUnits_Rw (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime]
    (Kw : IntermediateField ℚ_[q] (PadicAlgCl q)) [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[q] Kw] :
    ∃ e f : ℕ, 0 < e ∧ 0 < f ∧
      Ideal.span {((q : ℕ) : Rw q Kw)} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Rw q Kw) ^ e ∧
      Nat.card (IsLocalRing.ResidueField (Rw q Kw)) = q ^ f ∧
      e * f = Module.finrank ℚ_[q] Kw ∧
      (∀ k : ℕ, e < k → (principalUnits (Rw q Kw) k).map (powMonoidHom q) = principalUnits (Rw q Kw) (k + e)) ∧
      (∀ k : ℕ, e < k → ∀ ζ ∈ principalUnits (Rw q Kw) k, ζ ^ q = 1 → ζ = 1) := by sorry
